10
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:12.000
<v Grace Hopper>By region meaning the sales regions, or the billing regions? Because those don't line up.</v>

11
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
<v Ada Lovelace>I think sales regions. That's what the rest of the deck uses.</v>

12
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Grace Hopper>Okay. I can pull that. It's going to take me a bit, we've never cut churn that way before. But yeah, I'll get the churn by region numbers together for the QBR.</v>

13
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.000
<v Ada Lovelace>You've got three weeks.</v>

14
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:46.000
<v Grace Hopper>Are we defining churn the same way finance does? Because I think they have a version of this. They showed a churn slide last quarter.</v>

15
00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.000
<v Ada Lovelace>Might be worth looking at.</v>

16
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.000
<v Grace Hopper>Yeah, maybe.</v>

17
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:01.000
<v Ada Lovelace>Okay. The weekly deck. Honestly, somebody should look at whether we even need it anymore. I don't think anyone reads it.</v>

18
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:10.000
<v Grace Hopper>I've wondered the same thing. It'd be nice to have this stuff in Slack instead of a deck nobody opens.</v>

19
00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:16.000
<v Ada Lovelace>Maybe. Let's park that, we don't have time to redesign reporting right now.</v>

20
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:32.000
<v Grace Hopper>One more on data quality. We've still got all those test accounts in the customer table showing up in the counts. A few hundred? They all have the internal email domain, so they're easy to spot.</v>

21
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.000
<v Ada Lovelace>We could probably just filter those out.</v>

22
00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.000
<v Grace Hopper>Probably. Not urgent though.</v>

23
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:59.000
<v Ada Lovelace>The other thing is the revenue metric. Every team has a slightly different number and I keep getting asked which one is right. Let me just write down the definition we're actually using, so we have one place to point people. I'll put it in Confluence.</v>

24
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.000
<v Grace Hopper>Perfect, that'd help.</v>

25
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.000
<v Grace Hopper>Oh, before I forget. The Europe numbers.</v>

26
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.000
<v Ada Lovelace>What about them?</v>

27
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:22.000
<v Grace Hopper>I'm not sure whether the Europe rollup includes the reseller channel or not. If it does, the regional churn cut is going to look wrong and Sanjay will catch it.</v>

28
00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.000
<v Ada Lovelace>That would be bad in front of the board.</v>

29
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:35.000
<v Grace Hopper>Yeah. I'll check whether reseller is in the Europe rollup before I build the churn cut. Shouldn't take long.</v>

30
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:38.000
<v Ada Lovelace>Okay, good.</v>

31
00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:44.000
<v Grace Hopper>Are we still thinking about moving off the current BI tool next year?</v>

32
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:49.000
<v Ada Lovelace>It comes up every planning cycle. I don't think anything's decided.</v>

33
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.000
<v Grace Hopper>Fair enough.</v>

34
00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.000
<v Ada Lovelace>Alright, anything else? No? Thanks.</v>
